From 32d3a80962336d56d992837cc53e2c14f44ea41a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: burnoutIA <72673971+burnoutIA@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:39:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] harn: MTP coarse low-bit draft head over the full vocabulary
 with exact rerank (LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_COARSE=K)

With --spec-draft-mtp-vocab N > 0 and LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_COARSE=K, the MTP drafter scores every token with a
low-bit copy of the LM head (LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_COARSE_TYPE, default q2_K; q2_0 measured best), built once on the
CPU at load, then rescores the best K exactly against the original head. The draft keeps the full vocabulary's
acceptance at the cost of a small head; the target verifies with its own untouched head, so outputs follow the
same distribution.

R9700, Qwen3.8-27B Uncensored Q4_K_M, 10 seeds, 256 tokens (code / prose tok/s, prose acceptance):
  MTP3, vocab 98304       88.8 / 48.2 / 0.314
  MTP3, full vocab        82.7 / 50.0 / 0.386
  MTP3, coarse q2_0 K=64  88.7 / 53.4 / 0.382
  adaptive <=9 + ngram, vocab 98304   115.4 / 43.0
  adaptive <=9 + ngram, coarse q2_0   115.1 / 47.4
K = 16, 64 and 256 measure the same. Load time +4.5 s (requantization).
